{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Uue3Vza3gz5nLr1YsUBCUo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey information from the project:\n\n**Current MVP data (SciERC, Qwen3-8B ft_002_v2, N=8):**\n- NER: rho_sj = 0.38 (full), rho_fk = 0.26-0.34, SJ > FK consistently, headroom ~10-17pp, greedy F1 ~0.66\n- RE: rho_sj = 0.24 (full, FAIL), cond rho_sj = 0.32, compound error issue confirmed\n\n\n- The RE components are all performing similarly weak, with head_sj rho around 0.21\n\nLooking at the planned experiments, I'm organizing them into two priority phases: P0 covers the foundational work across NER datasets and RE diagnostics, while P1 focuses on scaling and stratification. The core tension I'm navigating is positioning this as primarily a NER paper with RE serving as a diagnostic tool, while still needing to validate across multiple datasets.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the key uncertainties: whether N=16 actually improves the correlation coefficient on SciERC, whether the NER generalization holds across CoNLL-2003 and OntoNotes, whether the single model family approach is limiting us, and whether the cross-dataset results will be consistent.\n\nI'm mapping out three outcome scenarios. In the best case, N=16 pushes the rho past 0.40 on SciERC, both cross-dataset experiments show SJ outperforming FK with similar correlations, the adaptive compute demo yields meaningful F1 improvements, and the RE analysis provides clear insights. The median scenario has N=16 improving rho only marginally to around 0.38-0.40, mixed cross-dataset results with one working well and one weaker, smaller advantages for SJ on some datasets, and messier RE diagnostics. The worst case is that N=16 doesn't improve rho at all.\n\nLooking at the actual numbers from my pilot experiments, the current SciERC baseline shows rho of 0.3825 for SJ versus 0.259 for FK, with a gap of 0.1235. The greedy F1 is 0.6671 and oracle is 0.7756, leaving 0.1085 headroom. For N=16, I'm expecting rho could potentially reach 0.42-0.48 if more samples improve estimation, stay in the 0.38-0.42 range as a median outcome, or potentially drop to 0.35-0.39 in the worst case. Now I need to think through what the cross-dataset results might look like.\n\nThe cross-dataset experiments show a more mixed picture. In the best case, both new datasets maintain rho above 0.35 with SJ outperforming FK by 5+ percentage points, though one dataset might show stronger signal than the other. In the worst case, rho drops below 0.30 on new datasets and the SJ advantage disappears entirely. For the adaptive compute experiments, I'm looking at potential F1 gains of 3-5 points over greedy selection in the best scenario, 1-2 points as a median outcome, and less than 1 point in the worst case where it's not meaningfully better than FK.\n\nThis shapes how I frame the narrative. The strongest version claims that structural self-consistency is a robust, general confidence signal across multiple datasets and scaling conditions. The more cautious version acknowledges that some datasets show weaker effects and I'd need to soften the generalizability claims.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the key metrics that matter most for the story. The flagship result is the NER rho on SciERC with N=16, then I need to track how that holds up across other datasets, the actual rho difference between SJ and FK, the F1 gains from adaptive compute, and whether the conditional rho on relation extraction supports the broader claims. Let me nail down what the best-case numbers actually look like. Now I'm looking at the worst-case performance bounds and refining the metric ranges to ensure they're properly ordered and overlapping at the boundaries. I need to make sure the best, median, and worst scenarios have consistent ranges across all the evaluation criteria, particularly for the rho_sj metrics and the cross-dataset performance deltas. Now I'm looking at the performance ranges for the conditional model, and they align well with the other metrics. Time to generate the YAML configuration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11791,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11791},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0bfddaa4-e6b1-4892-a29f-4918f38f665f","uuid":"4e3f70b8-329d-423a-9422-09e18a0841bf"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Uue3Vza3gz5nLr1YsUBCUo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"NER structural consistency generalizes across datasets and scales with N; diagnostic RE story is clean\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"N=16 materially improves rho estimation (rho_sj > 0.42 on SciERC NER)\"\n      - \"SJ > FK advantage replicates on both CoNLL-2003 and OntoNotes with comparable effect size\"\n      - \"SJ-based best-of-N selection yields practical F1 gain over greedy (≥3pp)\"\n      - \"RE conditional analysis cleanly separates capability-gap vs uncertainty instances; diagnostic claim needs no caveats\"\n    number_ranges:\n      ner_rho_sj_scierc_n16: [0.42, 0.50]\n      ner_rho_sj_crossdataset_min: [0.35, 0.45]\n      sj_minus_fk_delta_crossdataset_min: [0.06, 0.15]\n      adaptive_compute_f1_gain_over_greedy: [3.0, 6.0]\n      re_cond_rho_sj: [0.35, 0.42]\n      ner_oracle_headroom_n16: [0.12, 0.18]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Original framing 完全成立。Claim 1 用三数据集 + N-scaling curve + adaptive compute\n      F1 gain 构成完整证据链，reviewer 无法质疑 generalization。Claim 2 的 RE diagnostic\n      作为 principled boundary condition 收尾，component decomposition + temperature\n      analysis 提供机制解释。标题可以用 \"Structural Self-Consistency Enables Test-Time\n      Scaling for Entity-Level IE\"。冲 EMNLP Main 有信心。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"SciERC NER 结果稳固但跨数据集效果参差；RE diagnostic 可讲但不够 crisp\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"N=16 rho_sj 小幅提升或持平（0.38-0.43），不构成 dramatic improvement\"\n      - \"跨数据集中一个复现良好（SJ > FK ≥5pp），另一个效果偏弱（delta < 5pp 或 rho_sj < 0.30）\"\n      - \"Adaptive compute gain 存在但modest（1-3pp），reviewer 会质疑 practical significance\"\n      - \"RE conditional analysis 方向对但 rho 值不高，boundary condition 论证需要额外 caveats\"\n    number_ranges:\n      ner_rho_sj_scierc_n16: [0.38, 0.43]\n      ner_rho_sj_crossdataset_min: [0.25, 0.36]\n      sj_minus_fk_delta_crossdataset_min: [0.02, 0.08]\n      adaptive_compute_f1_gain_over_greedy: [1.0, 3.5]\n      re_cond_rho_sj: [0.28, 0.36]\n      ner_oracle_headroom_n16: [0.08, 0.13]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Claim 1 需降级：从 \"SJ is a general strong signal\" 收窄为 \"SJ is a consistently\n      better signal than FK, with effect size varying by dataset characteristics\"。\n      弱数据集不丢掉，而是作为 analysis 素材——分析什么数据集特性（entity density、type\n      granularity、label noise）影响 SJ 效果。Claim 2 不变但需要加 \"the boundary is\n      fuzzy\" 的 caveat。Adaptive compute 从 headline result 降为 supporting experiment。\n      可能需要补一个 exp-007（multi-model）来弥补跨数据集的弱点。标题软化为 \"When Does\n      Structural Self-Consistency Work? An Empirical Study on IE Test-Time Scaling\"。\n      EMNLP Main 偏紧，Findings 是 realistic target。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"跨数据集 NER 未复现 SJ 优势；N=16 未提升 rho；核心方法论 claim 不成立\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"N=16 对 rho_sj 无提升甚至下降（noise 未被 averaging out），rho 停留在 0.33-0.39\"\n      - \"CoNLL/OntoNotes 上 SJ 无显著优势（delta < 3pp 或 FK 反超），SciERC 结果是 dataset-specific artifact\"\n      - \"Adaptive compute F1 gain < 1.5pp，与 random selection 无统计显著差异\"\n      - \"RE diagnostic 本身也变得不 interesting——如果 NER 的 SJ 优势不 robust，boundary condition 论证失去锚点\"\n    number_ranges:\n      ner_rho_sj_scierc_n16: [0.33, 0.39]\n      ner_rho_sj_crossdataset_min: [0.10, 0.28]\n      sj_minus_fk_delta_crossdataset_min: [-0.03, 0.04]\n      adaptive_compute_f1_gain_over_greedy: [0.0, 1.5]\n      re_cond_rho_sj: [0.20, 0.30]\n      ner_oracle_headroom_n16: [0.06, 0.11]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 全部废弃。不能再 claim \"SJ is better than FK for IE\"。Reframe 方向：\n      转为 negative-result-driven analytical paper——\"Why Self-Consistency Fails as a\n      Confidence Signal for Structured Prediction\"。新 storyline：(1) 系统性地测试了\n      consistency-based confidence 在 IE 上的表现，(2) 发现即使 SJ 在单数据集上优于 FK，\n      该优势不跨数据集迁移，(3) 通过 error decomposition 和 dataset characteristic\n      analysis 解释失败原因（entity type granularity、annotation noise、output space\n      complexity），(4) 给出 practitioner guideline：什么条件下 consistency signal 可能\n      有效。这仍然是 EMNLP-caliber contribution——venue 明确欢迎 well-analyzed negative\n      results。但需要大幅增加 analysis depth 来补偿缺失的 positive result，exp-009\n      (capability stratification) 和 exp-005 (temperature sensitivity) 从 supporting\n      升级为 core experiments。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11791,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11791},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0bfddaa4-e6b1-4892-a29f-4918f38f665f","uuid":"edc8049a-0a5d-4151-bca1-6753dcab6d2d"}
